dict(task="3.5",
stem="A recipe website runs a copy of its application in two AWS Regions. The owners want visitors' DNS lookups to send them to the primary Region, and to send them to the second Region automatically if health checks show the primary is down. Which service does this?",
options=["Amazon Route 53", "Amazon CloudFront", "AWS Direct Connect", "AWS Transit Gateway"], answer="A",
expl="Route 53 is AWS's DNS service; with failover routing and health checks it answers with the primary Region's address while it is healthy and with the second Region's when it isn't. CloudFront is tempting because it's global and sits in front of websites, but it caches and delivers content from edge locations; answering DNS lookups is Route 53's job. Direct Connect and Transit Gateway connect networks.",
links=[("07-connecting-it/03-names-and-the-edge.md", "Route 53 answers \"where is it?\", and it can choose the answer")]),
